TICKET-306: Document the coverage-gated backend test command

Priority: P2 · Estimate: 0.5 pt · Depends on: 301
TICKET-301 added `npm run test:coverage` as the backend command CI actually gates on (per-file ≥ 80% over `src/domain`). `npm test` still runs the suite but skips the coverage threshold, so a contributor following README.md or CLAUDE.md can go green locally and red in CI.

Acceptance criteria

- README.md "Everyday commands" table lists `npm run test:coverage` as the command that matches CI, with `npm test` kept as the fast iteration command
- CLAUDE.md command table gains a "Run tests with coverage gate" row for the backend column
- Both files say explicitly that the coverage gate applies to `backend/src/domain` only
